ng} می‌برد؛ مدافع کناری برای بستن فضا جلو می‌آید.","{creator} کنار خط صاحب توپ است؛ یک هم‌تیمی برای حمایت نزدیک می‌شود.","بازی به جناح {wing} کشیده شده؛ «{team}» دنبال راهی برای ارسال است.","{creator} سرعت می‌گیرد؛ سمت {wing} دفاع حریف کمی باز شده است.","{creator} در کناره توپ را با مدافع کناری ردوبدل می‌کند؛ «{team}» سعی دارد از جناح {wing} دو به یک بسازد.","{creator} پشت مدافع کناری حرکت می‌کند؛ یک پاس به خط کناری، دفاع را به سمت {wing} می‌کشاند."],"central":["«{team}» توپ را بین خطوط می‌چرخاند؛ {creator} دنبال یک روزنه است.","{creator} توپ را به جلو می‌برد؛ چند بازیکن اطراف محوطه جابه‌جا می‌شوند.","چند پاس کوتاه از «{team}»؛ دفاع باید مراقب حرکت بدون توپ باشد.","{creator} بازی را از میانه بازسازی می‌کند؛ هنوز مسیر پاس نهایی باز نیست."],"long":["توپ به پشت محوطه می‌رسد؛ مدافعان کمی عقب نشسته‌اند.","«{team}» فضا پیدا کرده؛ {target} از فاصلهٔ دور دروازه را نگاه می‌کند.","{creator} به جای ارسال، توپ را پشت محوطه نگه می‌دارد.","دفاع راه نفوذ را بسته؛ شاید «{team}» از راه دور امتحان کند."],"direct":["یک توپ بلند از «{team}»؛ بازیکنان برای نبرد هوایی جلو می‌روند.","«{team}» بازی را بی‌معطلی به زمین حریف می‌برد؛ توپ در هواست.","{target} مدافع را پشت سر خود نگه داشته؛ توپ بلند به سمت او می‌آید.","خط دفاع «{team}» توپ را مستقیم به جلو فرستاده؛ رقابت برای توپ دوم شروع می‌شود."],"through":["توپ لو رفته؛ «{team}» فرصت دارد قبل از برگشت دفاع حمله کند.","{creator} رو به جلو می‌چرخد؛ {target} آمادهٔ فرار از پشت دفاع است.","دفاع هنوز مرتب نشده؛ «{team}» با چند نفر جلو می‌آید.","یک انتقال سریع از «{team}»؛ فاصلهٔ خطوط حریف زیاد شده است."],"dribble":["{target} در موقعیت تک‌به‌تک با مدافع صاحب توپ شده است.","«{team}» توپ را به {target} می‌رساند؛ فضای کوچکی برای دریبل هست.","{target} با توپ رو به مدافع می‌ایستد؛ هم‌تیمی‌ها مسیر را باز می‌کنند."],"cutback":["«{team}» به خط عرضی نزدیک شده؛ {creator} دنبال یک پاس رو به عقب است.","{creator} از کناره به محوطه نزدیک می‌شود؛ {target} پشت مدافع منتظر است.","دفاع به سمت دروازه عقب می‌رود؛ پشت نقطهٔ پنالتی فضایی باز شده است."]},"action":{"cross":["{creator} یک قدم از مدافع فاصله می‌گیرد و ارسال می‌کند؛ {target} به سمت توپ می‌رود.","توپ از سمت {wing} بلند می‌شود؛ {target} با مدافع برای جای‌گیری رقابت می‌کند.","{creator} ارسال تندی روی محوطه می‌فرستد؛ {target} خودش را به مسیر توپ می‌رساند.","یک ارسال به تیر دوم؛ {target} برای ضربهٔ سر بلند می‌شود."],"central":["{creator} یک پاس کوتاه بین دو مدافع می‌فرستد؛ {target} برای کنترل توپ قدم جلو می‌گذارد.","یک پاس و حرکت سریع؛ توپ به سمت {target} در محوطه می‌رود.","{creator} با یک پاس رو به جلو خط دفاع را امتحان می‌کند؛ {target} می‌چرخد.","{target} بین مدافعان جا می‌گیرد؛ توپ زمینی از {creator} به او نزدیک می‌شود."],"long":["{target} توپ را روی پایش تنظیم می‌کند؛ مدافع برای بستن زاویه می‌دود.","{target} یک قدم جلو می‌رود و پای شوتش را عقب می‌برد.","توپ جلوی پای {target} می‌افتد؛ فرصت یک شوت از پشت محوطه.","{target} تصمیم به شوت می‌گیرد؛ دروازه‌بان کمی جلوتر از خط ایستاده است."],"through":["{creator} پاس را از میان مدافعان رد می‌کند؛ {target} سرعت می‌گیرد.","{target} به سمت فضای خالی می‌دود؛ توپ در عمق ارسال می‌شود.","یک پاس عمقی به {target}؛ مدافع برای رسیدن به او برمی‌گردد.","{creator} در آخرین لحظه پاس می‌دهد؛ {target} پشت دفاع فرار می‌کند."],"direct":["{target} زیر توپ جا می‌گیرد و برای کنترل آن با مدافع درگیر می‌شود.","توپ بلند پایین می‌آید؛ {target} سعی می‌کند آن را با سینه مهار کند.","{target} برای توپ دوم جلو می‌رود؛ دفاع هنوز توپ را دور نکرده است.","نبرد شانه‌به‌شانه برای توپ؛ {target} به سمت محوطه فشار می‌آورد."],"dribble":["{target} بدنش را به یک سمت می‌برد و توپ را از سمت دیگر رد می‌کند؛ {defender} پا جلو می‌گذارد.","{target} با تغییر سرعت به سمت محوطه می‌رود؛ {defender} همراه اوست.","یک سر توپ از {target}؛ آیا می‌تواند از {defender} عبور کند؟"],"cutback":["{creator} توپ را از کنار خط عرضی به عقب می‌فرستد؛ {target} به سمت آن می‌دود.","پاس زمینی به پشت مدافعان برمی‌گردد؛ {target} برای ضربهٔ اول آماده می‌شود.","{creator} پاس کات‌بک را می‌فرستد؛ {target} و {defender} برای توپ جلو می‌روند.","{creator} به‌جای توپ بلند، پاس زمینی را به عقب می‌فرستد؛ {target} از پشت خط میانه وارد محوطه می‌شود."]},"interception":{"default":["{defender} مسیر توپ را می‌خواند و حمله را قطع می‌کند.","مدافع زودتر می‌رسد؛ {defender} توپ را از منطقهٔ خطر دور می‌کند.","{defender} در آخرین لحظه پا جلو می‌گذارد؛ فرصت از دست رفت.","پاس نهایی به مقصد نمی‌رسد؛ {defender} توپ را پس می‌گیرد.","{creator} پاس را کمی سنگین می‌فرستد؛ {defender} زودتر می‌رسد و توپ را می‌گیرد.","{target} برای کنترل توپ می‌چرخد اما لمس اولش بلند می‌شود؛ دفاع فرصت را از او می‌گیرد.","فشار حریف جواب می‌دهد؛ توپ از پای {creator} جدا می‌شود و حمله نیمه‌کاره می‌ماند."]},"goal":{"default":["{target} ضربه را می‌زند... گل! توپ از دروازه‌بان عبور کرد!","{target} می‌زند... داخل دروازه! بازیکنان «{team}» برای شادی گل دور هم جمع می‌شوند.","ضربهٔ {target} به سمت دروازه... گل! این بار دفاع کاری از دستش برنیامد.","گل برای «{team}»! {target} فرصت را با یک ضربهٔ دقیق تمام کرد!"]},"save":{"default":["{target} می‌زند... دروازه‌بان با نوک انگشت‌ها توپ را مهار می‌کند!","ضربهٔ {target} به سمت دروازه... واکنش عالی دروازه‌بان!","{target} ضربه را می‌زند؛ دروازه‌بان خودش را به توپ می‌رساند و آن را جمع می‌کند.","دروازه‌بان زاویه را بسته؛ ضربهٔ {target} به او می‌خورد و مهار می‌شود."]},"miss":{"default":["{target} می‌زند... توپ با فاصلهٔ کمی از کنار تیر رد می‌شود.","ضربهٔ {target} دقت کافی ندارد؛ توپ بالای دروازه می‌رود.","{target} تعادلش را موقع ضربه از دست می‌دهد؛ توپ بیرون می‌رود.","فرصت برای {target}... ضربه به بیرون! خودش هم از این پایان راضی نیست."]},"woodwork":{"default":["{target} می‌زند... اوه! صدای تیر دروازه بلند می‌شود!","ضربهٔ {target} از دروازه‌بان رد می‌شود... به تیر می‌خورد و بیرون می‌رود!","چه فرصتی برای {target}... توپ به تیر افقی می‌خورد!","{target} ضربه را می‌زند... تیر دروازه مانع گل می‌شود!"]}},"leagues":{"premier-league":"انگلستان","laliga":"اسپانیا","ligue-1":"فرانسه","serie-a":"ایتالیا","bundesliga":"آلمان","saudi-pro-league":"عربستان","super-lig":"ترکیه","mls":"آمریکا و کانادا","brasileirao":"برزیل"},"highlightCount":10,"commentaryMinMs":8000,"commentaryMaxMs":12000}$galactic$::jsonb,$galactic${"ratings":"Farsidle editorial gameplay traits; not EA or official ratings","rosterAsOf":"2026-11-03","traitsUpdated":"2026-11-03","notes":"# کهکشانی starter player pack\n\nCreated 2026-10-30. File: `players.json`.\n\nThe original v1 pool contained 298 real male players selected from 13 official men's first-team squad pages across the five requested leagues. Version 2 has 299 players after adding Kevin De Bruyne from Napoli. This is a deliberately selected starter pool, NOT a complete league database. The roster is a snapshot of the public pages accessed on 2026-10-30; those pages can change and several explicitly label 2026/27. Do not present this as a permanent live transfer feed or as independently audited registration data. Loaned-out sections were excluded where shown. Club names are editorial display names.\n\n## Primary roster sources accessed\n\n| Club | League | Public official source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Liverpool | Premier League | https://www.liverpoolfc.com/teams/mens-team?position=all |\n| Chelsea | Premier League | https://www.chelseafc.com/en/teams/mens-profiles |\n| Manchester City | Premier League | https://shop.mancity.com/en/lifestyle/men/ |\n| Barcelona | LaLiga | https://www.fcbarcelona.com/en/football/first-team/players |\n| Real Madrid | LaLiga | https://www.realmadrid.com/en-US/football/first-team/players |\n| Paris Saint-Germain | Ligue 1 | https://www.psg.fr/en/mens-football/squad |\n| Monaco | Ligue 1 | https://www.asmonaco.com/en/pros/players |\n| Marseille | Ligue 1 | https://www.om.fr/en/team/men |\n| Bayern Munich | Bundesliga | https://fcbayern.com/en/teams/first-team |\n| Borussia Dortmund | Bundesliga | https://www.bvb.de/de/de/mannschaften/fussball/maenner.html |\n| Inter | Serie A | https://www.inter.it/en/teams/first-team |\n| Juventus | Serie A | https://www.juventus.com/en/teams/first-team-men/squad/ |\n| AC Milan | Serie A | https://www.acmilan.com/en/teams/men-first-team |\n\nCorroborating official sources inspected:\n- Liverpool September 3, 2026 registered-squad announcement: https://lfcbeta.liverpoolfc.com/es/noticias/liverpool-submit-premier-league-squad-list-2026-27\n- Chelsea Premier League squad: https://www.premierleague.com/en/clubs/8/chelsea/squad?se=363\n- Dortmund Bundesliga squad: https://www.bundesliga.com/de/bundesliga/clubs/borussia-dortmund/profil\n- Juventus official store squad: https://store.juventus.com/ec/men-team\n- Inter official store squad: https://store.inter.it/se/men-team\n\nCity's source is the official club shop's men's-team player navigation, not a full position-verified football resource. Its names/club membership are shown there; detailed football positions below remain editorial. No photos, badges, logos, EA cards, biographies, or source-specific written descriptions are included in this pack.\n\n## Positions and identities\n\nNames and current club membership were checked against the listed public roster pages. Most pages use only broad goalkeeper/defender/midfielder/forward groups. Detailed positions GK/CB/LB/RB/DM/CM/AM/LW/RW/ST and secondary eligibility are EDITORIAL gameplay judgments based on recognizable playing roles, not claimed verbatim official position data. Primary role appears first. Stable IDs are normalized name slugs, independent of clubs. Real-world name collisions in future expansions should use a permanent distinguishing suffix rather than club names. No special-card duplicates.\n\nSome players use their familiar professional names (Rodri, Vanderson, Endrick, etc.) rather than full legal names. Names are Latin display forms. Persian transliterations are intentionally omitted until reviewed. A few official public pages contain recent transfers different from older seasons; the pack follows the accessed pages rather than old recollection.\n\n## Rating provenance: our own estimates, NOT EA\n\nEvery number is an ORIGINAL, provisional editorial game estimate. No EA numerical rating was imported or copied. No provider's match rating or statistical performance score was imported. These ratings are not objectively measured current performance and must never be labeled EA FC, official, or licensed EA ratings.\n\nRecommended user-facing attribution: «امتیازها برآورد اختصاصی فارسیدل برای این بازی هستند.»\n\nOverall values (62–94 in this pack) were manually estimated to create a usable range between elite, established, rotation and young players. Ability fields are generated from primary-position templates around that custom overall, with deterministic small differences and individual editorial adjustments for recognizable styles (for example, Kane has lower pace and stronger passing; Haaland has stronger physical play; Alexander-Arnold has stronger passing; modern distributing goalkeepers have stronger passing). This does NOT incorporate up-to-date season form, current injury status, real stamina tests, or professional scouting data.\n\nOutfield template offset order: pace, shooting, passing, dribbling, defending, physical, stamina, goalkeeping. Values are clamped 8–97; name-based deterministic jitter ranges −3 to +3.\n- CB: −13, −40, −13, −20, +2, +3, −5, −72\n- LB/RB: +5, −26, −6, −3, −2, −6, +1, −72\n- DM: −9, −20, 0, −5, 0, 0, +4, −72\n- CM: −6, −12, +3, 0, −17, −8, +3, −72\n- AM: −1, −5, +3, +5, −41, −16, −2, −72\n- LW/RW: +9, −4, −4, +5, −46, −17, −3, −72\n- ST: 0, +5, −15, −6, −48, 0, −7, −72\n- GK outfield fields: −45, −62, −32, −48, −59, −8, −25; numerical goalkeeping equals custom overall.\n\nGK records additionally contain goalkeeperSkills {diving, handling, kicking, reflexes, positioning}, around custom overall with offsets 0/−1/−3/+2/0 and small deterministic differences. These are also our own estimates. All players have a numeric goalkeeping field for a simple common engine interface.\n\nThe checked-in `players.json` is the reviewable source of the starter pool. Edit a new version when expanding; do not overwrite the frozen dataset of existing rooms.\n\n## Coverage and limits\n\nLeague counts: Premier League 72; LaLiga 46; Ligue 1 64; Bundesliga 46; Serie A 70.\nPrimary-role counts: GK 39, CB 59, LB 27, RB 18, DM 17, CM 47, AM 24, ST 31, RW 18, LW 18.\nThe 298 unique records comfortably exceed 8 × 11 picks and include adequate goalkeepers, center-backs, fullbacks, midfielders and attackers for common formations. Engine should still enforce legal draft completion and position availability.\n\nPublic source visibility is not a blanket commercial data license. This starter pack includes minimal factual identity/club information plus original numeric gameplay estimates, with no copied EA ratings or visual assets. Provider contracts and paid subscriptions are not required or used for this local prototype. If later using EA values or a full automated external feed, inspect its reuse terms separately.\n\nFreeze a roster/version snapshot when a room starts; later content edits should not change active tournaments. This recommendation protects gameplay consistency, not currentness guarantees.\n\n\n## Version 2: tactical and physical traits\n\nThe current pool has 299 players; Kevin De Bruyne (Napoli, Serie A) was added from the official Napoli announcement and Serie A profile. Names remain English. Numeric ability values are hidden from the game UI and authenticated public player/lineup responses. The server retains them for individual skill comparisons rather than comparing an overall team rating.\n\n45 players have source-verified heights as of 2026-10-31, with URLs on each record. Unknown heights remain absent: the engine uses neutral internal reach alongside editorial heading and jumping, never an invented factual height. `traits-sources.md` records primary sources and limitations. Heading, jumping, crossing, long shots, free kicks, penalties, composure and discipline are original gameplay estimates, not measured official statistics or personality claims. Discipline starts from a neutral gameplay baseline with small seeded variation.\n\nCrossing combines delivery quality, position fit, chemistry, attacking heading/jumping/reach and the defending player's aerial ability. Physical height contributes only part of reach: it does not define heading skill. Long-shot tactics trade conversion probability for more completed shooting opportunities; central attacks meet resistance from a low block; counters use pace against the defensive line. Formation numbers and midfield/defensive occupancy change control and coverage. Pressing increases fatigue and booking risk. Red cards remove the player from later actions and the shootout, with no suspension in later tournament matches.\n\nChemistry is a disclosed game rule: nearby same-club links improve coordination; listed club rivalries reduce it. The Kevin De Bruyne/Thibaut Courtois pair has a fictional penalty requested for gameplay. It is not an assertion about their real private lives. Green/blue/yellow/red indicate coordination, not actual emotions. Chemistry has a bounded effect, while tactical matchups, skill, position, fatigue and chance remain important.\n\n## Version 3 expansion — 2026-11-03\n\n644 players across 34 clubs. Includes curated playable selections of 15–26 players per Premier League club (all 20 clubs listed in the official 2026/27 league directory), plus Atletico Madrid, AS Roma, Lazio and a fuller Napoli selection. Existing AC Milan, Inter, Juventus, Bayern Munich and Borussia Dortmund selections remain. This is a curated pool, not a complete registration list. Club membership was checked against these public first-team sources; precise tactical roles and all numerical abilities remain original editorial game values, not official scouting data. Existing player identities/skills are retained; verified transfers update their club rather than duplicating the player.\n\nAdditional roster sources accessed 2026-11-03:\n- https://www.premierleague.com/en/news/4725682 (all 20 clubs; 2026/27 published list)\n- https://en.atleticodemadrid.com/jugadores-primer-equipo\n- https://www.asroma.com/en/men/players-and-staff\n- https://www.sslazio.it/en/team/lazio/squadra\n- https://sscnapoli.it/en/team-2025-2026/ (official destination of /en/team/; season label retained here)\n\nNew players have role-based editorial skills with small deterministic variation; ratings are hidden in the draft, and random suggestions are uniformly sampled from available specialists, not ranked by rating. Unknown heights remain absent.\n\nV3 engine: 18 independent regulation opportunity times sampled from minutes 1–90 and sorted; six extra-time times from 91–120. Duplicated minutes intentionally allow clustered action. Total regulation pace stays about eight minutes, with 16 seconds per sequence shared among its stages. Match seeds make the timeline identical for all viewers. Events include cutbacks, dribbling duels, blocked shots, goalkeeper claims/sweeps, playable corners, parried shots/rebounds and occasional offside reviews with possible disallowed goals. Stats and scores reveal only as each scene happens. Old saved timelines remain unchanged, and v1/v2 rooms keep their prior generation behavior.\n\n## Version 4 — competition choices and match management (2026-11-03)\n\n728 curated players across 42 clubs and nine leagues. Added MLS, Saudi Pro League, Turkish Super Lig and Brazil's Serie A selections, including Lionel Messi, Cristiano Ronaldo, Victor Osimhen, Neymar, Luis Suarez, Son Heung-Min and Antoine Griezmann. Additional missing first-team players were checked against the existing source sheets, including Ousmane Diomande at Nottingham Forest and Marc Pubill's CB/RB roles. This is still a curated pool, not a promise of every registered player in nine full leagues. All numeric abilities and exact tactical roles are original editorial gameplay values; factual unknown heights remain absent.\n\nRefreshed/expanded primary sources:\n- https://www.premierleague.com/en/news/4725682 and https://www.premierleague.com/en/clubs/17/nottingham-forest/squad\n- https://www.atleticodemadrid.com/jugadores/marc-pubill-pages-2026-2027\n- https://www.realmadrid.com/en-US/football/first-team/players/yan-diomande (current 2026/27 page takes precedence over Leipzig's older signing/training reports)\n- https://www.galatasaray.org/en/pl/squad/48\n- https://www.spl.com.sa/en/teams/al-nassr/squad\n- https://www.spl.com.sa/en/teams/al-ahli/squad\n- https://www.spl.com.sa/en/teams/al-hilal/squad\n- https://www.mlssoccer.com/players/lionel-messi/\n- https://www.mlssoccer.com/players/luis-suarez/stats/\n- https://www.mlssoccer.com/players/son-heung-min/\n- https://www.mlssoccer.com/players/antoine-griezmann/\n- https://www.santosfc.com.br/santos-fc-e-neymar-jr-renovam-contrato-ate-o-fim-de-2026/\n\nDraft offers are generated and persisted on the server, not selected by the browser. For each XI, four slot bands center on good players and seven on average players, rotated per manager. Available specialists within the band are uniformly shuffled. One re-roll during the initial draft and one fresh credit per match can improve a slot; reopening, switching tabs and automatic replacements do not reset credits. A re-roll that cannot offer a higher-rated option is rejected without consuming its credit. Numerical ratings remain hidden.\n\nCup retains knockout extra time and penalties. League uses a single round robin with concurrent fixtures by round, odd-team rest rounds, 3/1/0 points, then GD, GF and mini-table head-to-head points among tied teams. Completely tied teams share a rank; no arbitrary champion is selected. League draws end at 90 minutes.\n\nV4 simulates the first half only, stores the exact first-half state privately, pauses for 120 seconds, then simulates the second half from the saved match-local setup. Managers may change formation, tactic and captain/penalty/free-kick responsibilities, swap positions, and replace up to five starters from the undrafted pool. Incoming players are reserved across the current round to prevent duplicate use. Sent-off players cannot be substituted or act later. Substitutes start their own stamina clock at minute 45. Original room XIs and responsibilities return for the next match.\n\nWeighted event participation replaces the striker-only priority: wings and midfielders contribute to finishing, while CBs and other advancing players contest corners. Tactics change route frequencies, possession, passing, chance construction and fatigue. Each corner and foul counted in stats has a narrated award/whistle. Commentary includes first-touch mistakes, misplaced passes, overlap play, cutbacks and varied outcomes. Captain status contributes a small 2.5% factor to that player's profile; set-piece assignments override automatic selections when the chosen player remains on the pitch.\n\n## Version 5 tuning (2026-11-03)\n\nThe 728-player roster is unchanged. V5 changes highlight selection and pacing: ten dangerous regulation chances, roughly 40% conversion for comparable teams, 8–12 seconds per commentary beat, an unresolved keeper-rush action, and playable first/second-half stoppage time. Numerical ratings remain private and all previous tactical/fit/chemistry/stamina factors feed the adjusted chance quality. No guaranteed consolation goal is inserted. Save-once halftime readiness is stored per match; both teams saving immediately generates the second half, with the halftime event shortened to the actual wait. Version snapshots preserve existing started games.\n\n\n## Version 6 — match performance and commentary readability\n\nCaptain/penalty/free-kick saves now use an unambiguous local variable in the validated action RPC. New v6 rooms retain v5 football probabilities and random seeds, with structured actor/provider/keeper IDs and team attribution on each revealed incident. No future events or private ability values are exposed. Commentary has 10–16 seconds per attacking line and additional independently sampled build-up details; the narration panel stays in document flow below the pitch, alongside a permanent incident log.\n\nMatch performance starts at 6.5 and is bounded 1–10. These are original simplified Farsidle performance scores, not official provider ratings and not an input to simulation. Goals add 0.85 for ST or 1.05 for other roles; assists 0.5; named completed key passes 0.08; goalkeeper saves 0.25; defensive corner clearances 0.08. Recovered poor controls subtract 0.12, misses 0.15 (missed penalties 0.65), yellow cards 0.25 and dismissals 1.2; conceded goals cost the keeper 0.22. Only revealed, attributed actions count: aggregate team pass totals are not fabricated into individual pass records. Scores are a lightweight game model, not a comprehensive real-world match analysis. Goals/card summaries use actor-team attribution, independently of the attacking team's narration color.\n\nTactical balance remains unchanged for review: role-weighted defence/midfield/attack, position fit, chemistry, fatigue, skill matchups and tactic multipliers shape control and conversion. Ten dangerous regulation highlights are shared between teams according to control/counter factors; tactics currently change type, share and conversion rather than the total highlight count. There is no continuous player-movement or individual marking engine. Base ability traits remain editorial estimates, many initially derived from custom overall templates; the simulation does not directly look up overall. Started v5 rooms keep their frozen generation behavior; new/lobby rooms use v6.\n"}$galactic$::jsonb,true)on conflict(version)do nothing;
update galactic_private.datasets set active=true where version='galactic-v6';
with upgraded as(update galactic_private.rooms set dataset_version='galactic-v6',version=version+1 where phase='lobby' and dataset_version<> 'galactic-v6' returning id)update galactic_private.members set ready=false where room_id in(select id from upgraded);
commit;
